Reduced operation needs a physical recovery condition (@cm-setback-recovery: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @clean-manufacturing, #source "../sources/Cleanroom-Programming-and-Energy-LBNL.lingua#r_36R5RS6HEWBTYN4SHCVPQNP12X", #source "../sources/Demand-Controlled-Cleanroom-Filtration-Faulkner-Fisk-Walton.lingua#r_2W1ADE030W9RFA8ATDKSYVT6XP", #clean-manufacturing "../../../engineering/mechanical-engineering-and-machine-design/service/Human-access-stored-energy-and-isolation.lingua#r_0FD90Y234EJ4QAT78JTCYQNTEE") { r_7QVBPV6BTRDD2V7WT9DFT0WMR8
**Read:** [Cleanroom programming and energy — Tschudi, Sartor and Xu](../sources/Cleanroom-Programming-and-Energy-LBNL.lingua#r_36R5RS6HEWBTYN4SHCVPQNP12X), control and part-load operation; [Demand-controlled cleanroom filtration — Faulkner, Fisk and Walton](../sources/Demand-Controlled-Cleanroom-Filtration-Faulkner-Fisk-Walton.lingua#r_2W1ADE030W9RFA8ATDKSYVT6XP), low-flow observations.

During reduced operation, sources, pressure paths, temperature, humidity and treatment can change together. Restarting fans does not instantly restore every surface and utility. A source-free exponential air purge is only one possible part of recovery.

Define the physical state needed before exposing a product or resuming a process. Measure recovery under the intended operating disturbance, including transfer and personnel movement. A low average concentration while empty does not establish the occupied condition.

**Work:** Compare two operating schedules using integrated energy and exposure, not only idle fan speed. Apply the earlier recovery equation where its assumptions hold, and identify a state it cannot predict. Explain what evidence is needed after an extended interruption, a filter change or changed process loading.

**Return:** [Clean manufacturing and contamination control — from familiar objects to controlled processes](../Clean-manufacturing-and-contamination-control.lingua#r_7D8SQ8BVQDZQBDBGC6DP0JAMZN).
